%%%
An explicit ellipticity estimate

$$`
c\lVert v\rVert^2\leq B(v,v)\qquad(c>0)
`

gives $`\lVert S_B\rVert\leq c^{-1}` and reduces the contraction condition to
the transparent smallness hypothesis $`K<c`. The threshold comes from the
Lax–Milgram operator bound.
:::

:::proof "methods.semilinear.contraction_coercivity" (uses := "methods.semilinear.contraction")
The coercivity estimate bounds the Lax–Milgram solution operator by $`c^{-1}`.
The inequality `K < c` therefore implies that its composition with the
nonlinear load is a strict contraction.
:::

On $`H^1_0(\Omega)` the abstract load is the Nemytskii load of a scalar
nonlinearity $`g`, and the threshold $`K<c` becomes a condition on $`g` alone.

:::theorem "methods.semilinear.dirichlet_contraction" (parent := "methods.semilinear_nonvariational") (lean := "SobolevSpace.GraphSpace.existsUnique_dirichlet_semilinear_of_lipschitz_lt_coercivity") (uses := "methods.dirichlet.semilinear_weak_solution")
